{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 4958062,
  "courseSlug": "remix-course",
  "courseTitle": "Remix.js - The Practical Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "34675888",
      "title": "Adding an Expense Data Model",
      "lectureOrder": 61,
      "videoOrder": 55,
      "sourceHash": "b1809f879725f56871b8015e9a8e2e4b12721786ef152408e73542afc17a310c",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.31,
          "end": 4.53,
          "en": "Now with Prisma installed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.53,
          "end": 8.01,
          "en": "it's time to tell Prisma how our data should look like",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.01,
          "end": 11.43,
          "en": "because Prisma will manage that data for us under the hood",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.43,
          "end": 13.83,
          "en": "and it will talk to the database under the hood",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.83,
          "end": 16.863,
          "en": "and store the data there and fetch the data from there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.88,
          "end": 20.61,
          "en": "Now we do tell Prisma how our data looks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.61,
          "end": 23.46,
          "en": "like by going to the schema dot prisma file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.46,
          "end": 27.21,
          "en": "And then there you can type model, and then any name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.21,
          "end": 30.63,
          "en": "of your choice for that data model you want to define.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.63,
          "end": 32.97,
          "en": "And here in my case, I want to have expenses,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.97,
          "end": 36.63,
          "en": "so I will give that model a name of expense, not expenses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.63,
          "end": 38.31,
          "en": "but expense because even",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.31,
          "end": 40.47,
          "en": "though we will have multiple expenses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.47,
          "end": 43.047,
          "en": "we wanna model one single expense here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.047,
          "end": 44.62,
          "en": "And Prisma will then make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.615,
          "end": 47.633,
          "en": "that we can also handle multiple expenses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.261,
          "end": 51.24,
          "en": "Thereafter, you add curly braces,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.24,
          "end": 54,
          "en": "and then you can define your data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54,
          "end": 55.5,
          "en": "For example, by making sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 55.5,
          "end": 57.453,
          "en": "that every expense has a unique ID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 58.687,
          "end": 61.86,
          "en": "That ID in Prisma's world when using MongoDB,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 61.86,
          "end": 63.45,
          "en": "is generally a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 63.45,
          "end": 67.77,
          "en": "So it's some text and that has to start with a capital S.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 67.77,
          "end": 71.88,
          "en": "So here we define which field our expense data will have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 71.88,
          "end": 74.763,
          "en": "and which type of data it will be in that field.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 75.66,
          "end": 78.03,
          "en": "And then we have to add some annotations here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 78.03,
          "end": 80.91,
          "en": "for Prisma to store that data correctly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 80.91,
          "end": 83.13,
          "en": "in the MongoDB database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 83.13,
          "end": 86.13,
          "en": "And here in this schema dot prisma file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 86.13,
          "end": 89.91,
          "en": "we have to add an at ID annotation here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 89.91,
          "end": 92.22,
          "en": "And by the way, I'm getting some auto completion here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 92.22,
          "end": 96.3,
          "en": "because I installed the Prisma extension for VS code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 96.3,
          "end": 97.65,
          "en": "You can install that as well",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 97.65,
          "end": 101.03999999999999,
          "en": "of course to get this auto completion.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 101.03999999999999,
          "end": 103.203,
          "en": "But you don't need it to use Prisma.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 104.362,
          "end": 106.703,
          "en": "Prisma works without that extension as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 106.703,
          "end": 109.08,
          "en": "It's just convenient to have the extension.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 109.08,
          "end": 110.19,
          "en": "But here we have to add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 110.19,
          "end": 115.19,
          "en": "at ID after this string type annotation, then at default",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 115.595,
          "end": 119.82,
          "en": "and there we have to open and close parentheses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 119.82,
          "end": 122.61,
          "en": "and in those parentheses type auto to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 122.61,
          "end": 125.52,
          "en": "that essentially prisma ensures that when data is stored",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 125.52,
          "end": 129.21,
          "en": "in MongoDB, a new ID is generated automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 129.21,
          "end": 131.733,
          "en": "and we don't have to generate IDs manually.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 132.72,
          "end": 134.76,
          "en": "And then we add at map.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 134.76,
          "end": 139.68,
          "en": "And then in parenthesis, in double quotes underscore id.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 139.68,
          "end": 143.19,
          "en": "This simply ensures that Prisma will add an extra underscore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 143.19,
          "end": 146.79,
          "en": "ID field in our MongoDB database in which the idea",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 146.79,
          "end": 147.66,
          "en": "is stored.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 147.66,
          "end": 150.48,
          "en": "And then maps that to an ID field without a leading",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 150.48,
          "end": 154.17000000000002,
          "en": "underscore when we work with the data in our code here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 154.17000000000002,
          "end": 156.22,
          "en": "And that's just some convenience feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 157.503,
          "end": 160.195,
          "en": "When using MongoDB, the ID is typically stored",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 160.195,
          "end": 161.848,
          "en": "in an underscore ID field.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 161.848,
          "end": 164.47,
          "en": "That's why we store it like this in the database",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 164.47,
          "end": 166.847,
          "en": "but work with it like this in our code without",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 166.847,
          "end": 168.293,
          "en": "the underscore, which is more convenient.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 169.23,
          "end": 171.84,
          "en": "And then last by the least, we add another annotation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 171.84,
          "end": 174.81,
          "en": "at DB dot object id.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 174.81,
          "end": 178.56,
          "en": "And this is just the internal type that's used by MongoDB in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 178.56,
          "end": 180.03,
          "en": "their database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 180.03,
          "end": 182.25,
          "en": "Now these are details you don't need to memorize.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 182.25,
          "end": 184.41,
          "en": "It's not related to Remix.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 184.41,
          "end": 189.06,
          "en": "This is just some MongoDB prisma stuff going on here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 189.06,
          "end": 191.31,
          "en": "But with that, we'll make sure that every expense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 191.31,
          "end": 194.583,
          "en": "which we'll create will have an automatically generated ID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 195.72,
          "end": 198.6,
          "en": "Now of course, expenses should not just have IDs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 198.6,
          "end": 202.26,
          "en": "they should also have names or titles or however",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 202.26,
          "end": 203.64,
          "en": "you want to name that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 203.64,
          "end": 206.76,
          "en": "So here I'll add a title property to my expense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 206.76,
          "end": 208.953,
          "en": "data objects with which we'll work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 209.82,
          "end": 211.56,
          "en": "And this will also be of type screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 211.56,
          "end": 214.38,
          "en": "And here no special annotations are needed because",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 214.38,
          "end": 217.8,
          "en": "titles won't be auto-generated or anything like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 217.8,
          "end": 220.07999999999998,
          "en": "Instead, titles are simply text that will be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 220.07999999999998,
          "end": 221.433,
          "en": "stored in the database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 222.78,
          "end": 225.57,
          "en": "Now we also want to store the amount of the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 225.57,
          "end": 227.22,
          "en": "expense that we created.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 227.22,
          "end": 229.95,
          "en": "So if we bought a book for twelve ninety-nine",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 229.95,
          "end": 230.888,
          "en": "we wanna store that amount,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 230.888,
          "end": 233.523,
          "en": "twelve ninety-nine in the database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 234.39,
          "end": 238.26,
          "en": "Now that amount could be stored as plain text as a string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 238.26,
          "end": 241.8,
          "en": "but it probably makes more sense to store it as a float",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 241.8,
          "end": 244.77,
          "en": "so as a number with decimal places.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 244.77,
          "end": 247.743,
          "en": "And here we also don't need any special annotations.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 248.64,
          "end": 249.9,
          "en": "Now my expenses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 249.9,
          "end": 253.32,
          "en": "in this application also should have dates attached",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 253.32,
          "end": 257.04,
          "en": "to them so that we know when an expense occurred.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 257.04,
          "end": 260.25,
          "en": "And for that, I add a date field to every expense object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 260.25,
          "end": 262.89,
          "en": "And this will be of type date time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 262.89,
          "end": 265.59,
          "en": "So, it will be stored as a date in the database",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 265.59,
          "end": 268.473,
          "en": "and we'll work with it as a date in our code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 269.43,
          "end": 273.42,
          "en": "Last but not least, I'll also add a date added field",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 273.42,
          "end": 275.163,
          "en": "which is all of type date time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 276.044,
          "end": 278.90999999999997,
          "en": "and this will be a field that should be automatically set.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 278.90999999999997,
          "end": 280.949,
          "en": "Whenever we add a new expense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 280.949,
          "end": 282.03,
          "en": "we basically assign a timestamp",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 282.03,
          "end": 285.51,
          "en": "to the expense that tells us when that expense was added.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 285.51,
          "end": 287.223,
          "en": "So not when it occurred,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 288.069,
          "end": 289.87,
          "en": "that's the state field instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 289.87,
          "end": 293.37,
          "en": "But simply when we added this expense to the database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 293.37,
          "end": 296.97,
          "en": "And here, we add another annotation to automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 296.97,
          "end": 299.13,
          "en": "give this a default value so that we don't",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 299.13,
          "end": 302.94,
          "en": "have to manually set this value when we add a new expense.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 302.94,
          "end": 306,
          "en": "And here we can use this now function provided",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 306,
          "end": 309.012,
          "en": "by Prisma to basically add the current timestamp",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 309.012,
          "end": 312.42,
          "en": "to an expense when we create it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 312.42,
          "end": 314.73,
          "en": "Now here I just pressed the auto format shortcut to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 314.73,
          "end": 317.63,
          "en": "get this format, which is not required technically though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 318.559,
          "end": 321.462,
          "en": "And with that, we defined how an expense should look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 321.462,
          "end": 323.73,
          "en": "like in the database and in our code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 323.73,
          "end": 325.86,
          "en": "And of course you could have different definitions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 325.86,
          "end": 328.74,
          "en": "but that is what we'll use for this demo.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 328.74,
          "end": 331.59,
          "en": "And with that, we got this model defined.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 331.59,
          "end": 334.71,
          "en": "Now, we're pretty much done with the Prisma setup",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 334.71,
          "end": 336.54,
          "en": "and we can therefore now make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 336.54,
          "end": 339,
          "en": "that we actually create an expense that has",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 339,
          "end": 342.21,
          "en": "this shape whenever we submit this expense form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 342.21,
          "end": 346.053,
          "en": "which we already have in our application, this form here.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
